---
title: Hokkaido Milk Bread
image: https://i.pinimg.com/originals/49/30/35/493035af3dae80de6836ed3fbbe7dca0.jpg
source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tc3coiL36Cg
---

== Tangzhong ==

Mix @bread flour{40%g} with @water{200%g} in a sauce pan. Turn on medium heat and keep stirring until mixture thickens to a paste.

Refrigerate for ~{6%hours}. Bring out to room temperature ~{1%hour} before use.

== Bread ==

In a #stand mixer{} with the dough hook attatchment, gently mix @bread flour{580%g}(approximately 4 cups), @sugar{60%g}(approximately 1/4 cup), @salt{12%g}(approximately 2 tsp), @active dry yeast {10%g}, and @powdered dry milk{10%g}(approximately 2.5 tsp).

At low speed, mix in @milk{260%g}(approximately 1 cup and 2 tbsp), @egg{1}, and tangzhong so that no flour is visible.

Add @unsalted butter{50%g}(approximately 1/2 stick, room temperature) and continue to mix at low speed.

Slowly turn up the speed to high and mix until all dough sticks together.

Take the dough and fold it around and underneath itself, shaping a smooth ball. Place dough in a bowl, cover with plastic wrap, and let it rest for ~{40-60%minutes}.

> Test the dough by poking your finger down into the middle. If the dough does not spring back, it is ready.

Divide the dough into 6 equal parts (by weight). Take one piece of dough and fold it over itself. Turn it 90°, slap it on table and fold it over itself again. Using both hands, mold the dough into a ball. Repeat with rest of dough. Cover with plastic wrap and let it rest for ~{15%minutes}.

Roll each ball of dough out flat. Fold flatten dough using thirds. 

Turn 90°, and roll dough into a roll, pinching it together at the seam. Place 3 molded dough into a baking pan and let it rest/rise for ~{30%minutes}.

Create an egg wash by whisking @egg yolk{1} with @milk{1%splash}. Brush the dough with the egg wash and bake in the oven, preheated to 355°F for ~{25-30%minutes}.